The payloads are documentation examples, largely taken from GitHub Docs
(https://docs.github.com/en/webhooks/webhook-events-and-payloads; GitHub Docs
content is CC-BY-4.0, https://github.com/github/docs/blob/main/LICENSE).
Attribution: webhook payload examples by GitHub, Inc., via octokit/webhooks.
Most accounts are placeholders (octocat, Codertocat, noreply addresses), but
some examples name real public GitHub accounts (logins, ids, avatar and
profile URLs) as published in those docs; no e-mail address other than
noreply and placeholder ones is kept. GH Archive was not used: it has no data
licence and carries personal data.

sample.jsonl.zst holds all 329 payloads of the api.github.com directory (58
event types), one record per payload, with the event name added. It is a
subset of fields: the shared envelope (sender, repository, organization,
installation) plus issue, comment, pull_request, release, label and push
fields (ref, before, after, commits, head_commit, pusher); all other payload
fields are dropped. Timestamps (ISO strings, or Unix seconds in push events)
are normalised to UTC milliseconds. The tarball's ghes-31..35 directories are
only read when the full data is loaded (726 payloads).

Regenerate it with:

    go run ./cmd/fetch -dataset ghwebhooks
    go test ./datasets/ghwebhooks -update "$PWD/data/ghwebhooks/webhooks-examples-7.6.1.tgz"
